// Generated by tools/genref.java --jar <client.jar> --collision <scratch-dir>.
// Do not edit by hand.
//
// **Every collision box in a1.1.2**: each block the version constructs, crossed
// with all sixteen metadata values, asked through `addCollisionBoxesToList` --
// the same entry point `Entity.moveEntity` reaches through
// `World.getCollidingBoundingBoxes`. Sixteen is the whole domain of a metadata
// nibble, so this is the entire truth table rather than a sample of it.
//
// Coordinates are relative to the block's own corner, so a full cube is
// 0,0,0 -> 1,1,1. Boxes are listed in the order the original appends them.
//
// Measured facts worth not re-deriving:
//
//   * A box depends only on (id, metadata). Nothing consults a neighbour --
//     not the top half of a door, which reads its own low three bits and
//     ignores bit 8 entirely, and not a fence, which does not connect. That
//     is what lets mc::block::collisionBoxes be a pure function.
//   * Stairs are the only block that answers with more than one box.
//   * A ladder with metadata outside 2..5 sets no bounds at all, and in the
//     original answers with whatever the shared Block singleton was left
//     holding by the previous query. The generator restores each block's own
//     constructor bounds before every query, so what is recorded here is that
//     default rather than an artefact of iteration order.
//
// Regenerate with:
//   java tools/genref.java --jar <client.jar> --collision /tmp/genref-scratch
//     redirected to tests/collision_box_vectors.hpp

